<title>USA: BNH Bancshares Q1 March 31 net, shr fall.</title>
<headline>BNH Bancshares Q1 March 31 net, shr fall.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands except ratios and per share data)</p>
<p>				     ---THREE MONTH PERIOD ENDED---</p>
<p>				03/31/97	12/31/96	03/31/96</p>
<p>Net interest income	 $3,373	  $3,354	  $3,027</p>
<p>Provision for loan losses    326	     362	     576</p>
<p>Other income		     798	     815	     788</p>
<p>OREO expense			37		57		46</p>
<p>Operating expenses	   3,001	   3,242	   2,684</p>
<p>Income before tax		807	     508	     509</p>
<p>Provision (benefit) for income taxes</p>
<p>				    323	     161	    (225)</p>
<p>Net income			$484	    $347	    $734</p>
<p>Average Shares		 3,691	   3,682	   3,682</p>
<p>Common share data :</p>
<p>  Net income before tax    $0.22	   $0.14	   $0.14</p>
<p>  Net income(loss)	    0.13	    0.09	    0.20</p>
<p>  Book value		    6.98	    6.96	    4.34</p>
<p>NOTES: (1) Previous weighted average share data adjusted to reflect a 1 for 4 reverse stock split in May, 1996.</p>
<p>The company's net interest income rose 11.5 percent to $3,373,000 in Q1 1997, up from $3,027,000 in Q1 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name is BNH Bancshares Inc.</p>
</text>
